{"qid":"Q837","names":["Nepal"],"title":"Nepal","endonym":{"native":"नेपाल","lang":"ne"},"capsule":"The Kingdom of Nepal in its modern form emerged when Prithvi Narayan Shah of Gorkha completed the conquest of the Kathmandu Valley in 1768–1769, unifying a patchwork of Malla principalities into a single state; the Rana oligarchy dominated from 1846 to 1951. Nepal withstood British pressure during the Anglo-Nepalese War (1814–1816) and the resulting Sugauli Treaty fixed its current borders with British India, making it the only Himalayan state to maintain formal independence throughout the colonial era. The absolute monarchy was replaced by a constitutional system in 1990, and a decade of Maoist insurgency (1996–2006) culminated in the Comprehensive Peace Agreement and the abolition of the monarchy in 2008, establishing the Federal Democratic Republic of Nepal. The country remains a sovereign multi-ethnic federal republic today.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. Nepal's post-1816 borders are precisely defined by treaty; pre-unification and early Shah-period boundaries are reconstructed from historical chronicles and are approximate.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[{"label":"Britannica: Nepal","url":"https://www.britannica.com/place/Nepal"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Nepal","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nepal"}],"britannica":"place/Nepal","cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"Nepal","rulers":[{"qid":"Q4206839","name":"Bhimsen Thapa","start":1806,"end":1837,"image":"Bhimsen-thapa-portrait.jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Bhimsen-thapa-portrait.jpg?width=320","imageLicense":{"license":"Pu